e,"elType":"container"},{"id":"5db97a07","settings":{"text":"Request Service","align":"justify","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"BeVietnamPro-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":22,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"500","hover_color":"#FFFFFF","hover_animation":"shrink","border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"50","right":"50","bottom":"50","left":"50","isLinked":true},"text_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"18","right":"18","bottom":"18","left":"18","isLinked":false},"_element_width":"initial","_element_custom_width":{"unit":"px","size":250,"sizes":[]},"_flex_align_self":"center","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"713e9df"}],"custom_css":".elementor-nav-menu__align-justify .elementor-nav-menu--layout-horizontal .elementor-nav-menu>li:before{\n    content: \"\";\n    position: absolute;\n    background: #fff;\n    height: 8px;\n    width: 8px;\n    border-radius: 50px;\n    top: 50%;\n    left: 0;\n    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n}\n.elementor-nav-menu__align-justify .elementor-nav-menu--layout-horizontal .elementor-nav-menu>li:nth-child(1):before{\n    display: none;\n}","__globals__":{"button_background_hover_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary","button_text_color":"globals\/colors?id=1d0e19b5","border_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary","button_hover_border_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary","background_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"},"border_border":"solid","border_width":{"unit":"px","top":"2","right":"2","bottom":"2","left":"2","isLinked":true},"typography_text_transform":"capitalize","_margin":{"unit":"px","top":"40","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"link":{"url":"\/request-service\/","is_external":"","nofollow":"","custom_attributes":""}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"button","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2b624a97","settings":{"flex_direction":"column","content_width":"full","margin":{"unit":"px","top":"24","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"6e039fb"}]},"elements":[{"id":"2ab90e6e","settings":{"title":"Indoor Air Quality FAQs for Central Louisiana Homes","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"61f1bc6"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"64c50a06","settings":{"items":[{"item_title":"What does indoor air quality service include?","_id":"100d091"},{"item_title":"Why does indoor air quality matter in Central Louisiana?","_id":"f376a32"},{"item_title":"Do I need a dehumidifier or an air purifier?","_id":"6f7ee22"},{"_id":"6e545a4","item_title":"What is the ideal indoor humidity level?"},{"_id":"72cddbc","item_title":"What are the signs of poor indoor air quality?"},{"_id":"e919371","item_title":"How often should indoor air quality equipment be serviced?"}],"title_tag":"h3","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"068d9a8"}]},"elements":[{"id":"4afd6ca8","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"78109f2"}]},"elements":[{"id":"44644b63","settings":{"editor":"<p>Indoor air quality service includes filtration, air purification, humidity control, and ventilation. Together these remove airborne particles, manage moisture, and exchange stale air, which reduces allergens, odors, and the risk of mold in your home.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"12d4bf4"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"26948b21","settings":{"_title":"item #2","content_width":"full","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"64d1905"}]},"elements":[{"id":"1ea21c5a","settings":{"editor":"<p>Central Louisiana has high humidity for much of the year, which allows mold, dust mites, and bacteria to thrive indoors. Controlling humidity and filtration reduces those triggers and helps homes feel less sticky, even when the air conditioner is running.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"8c18aa1"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"ab438c4","settings":{"_title":"item #3","content_width":"full","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"a14f7ef"}]},"elements":[{"id":"1a563828","settings":{"editor":"<p>They solve different problems. A dehumidifier removes excess moisture to prevent mold and that damp, sticky feeling, while an air purifier removes airborne particles like dust, pollen, and dander. In humid climates, many homes benefit from both, and a technician can evaluate which your home needs most.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"1db10ec"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"63fc3c62","settings":{"_title":"Item #4","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"98b49e5"}]},"elements":[{"id":"7c728245","settings":{"editor":"<p>The recommended indoor relative humidity is between 30% and 50%. Above 50%, moisture encourages mold and dust mites; below 30%, air feels dry and can irritate skin and airways. A whole-home dehumidifier keeps humidity within this range automatically.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"1e32f5d"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"7cae2e26","settings":{"_title":"Item #5","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"b7ed8ea"}]},"elements":[{"id":"1570b2d0","settings":{"editor":"<p>Common signs include persistent stuffiness or sticky air, musty odors, worsening allergy or asthma symptoms, frequent dust buildup, and condensation on windows. Any of these can indicate a humidity, filtration, or ventilation problem worth having inspected.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"2aa4eca"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"955d594","settings":{"_title":"Item #6","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"921a7bf"}]},"elements":[{"id":"6d6404df","settings":{"editor":"<p>Air filters should generally be checked every 1 to 3 months and replaced as needed, while dehumidifiers, purifiers, and ventilation systems benefit from a professional check at least once a year. Homes with pets, allergies, or heavy use may need more frequent attention.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"30a103f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true}],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"nested-accordion","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"3e9aa62d","settings":{"text":"Divider","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"35a5253"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"divider","elType":"widget"},{"id":"532224e3","settings":{"title":"<a href=\"\/contact-us\/\">Schedule<\/a> Indoor Air Quality Service in Dry Prong, LA, and Surrounding Areas","header_size":"h3","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"25ada42"}],"_margin":{"unit":"px","top":"40","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetTyp